<title>ITALY: Banca PopMilano 1996 cons profit up 90 pct.</title>
<headline>Banca PopMilano 1996 cons profit up 90 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian banking group Banca Popolare di Milano (BPM) said 1996 consolidated profit rose 90.9 percent from 1995 to 264.5 billion lire.</p>
<p>Consolidated net assets rose to 2.33 trillion lire from 2.06 trillion, the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>Group interest income rose 2.2 percent to 1.26 trillion lire and operating income rose 5.7 percent to 1.94 trillion.</p>
<p>Group customer deposits rose 4.6 percent to 15.44 trillion lire and customer loans rose 4.8 percent to 17.02 trillion.</p>
<p>((-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589 ))</p>
